TB371FC-ArchLinux — third-party components

1. Linux kernel and device tree
   Files: boot_a.img, dtbo_a.img (inside the release image)
   License: GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note
   Source:  https://github.com/smith-dog/kernel-tb371fc  (4.19.325 bring-up tree)
            based on Lenovo's GPL release for TB371FC and
            https://github.com/lss4/android_kernel_lenovo_paladin
   The boot image is a repack: vendor-style 4.19.325 kernel, our own initramfs
   and Linux cmdline. Build configuration is published at
   docs/kernel/tb371fc-4.19.325.config; the license text is COPYING in the
   upstream tree.
   Written offer: if you need the source corresponding to this binary and it is
   not covered by the upstream repository, open an issue at
   https://github.com/jiimjiim/TB371FC-ArchLinux/issues and we will provide it.

2. Arch Linux ARM root filesystem (userdata.img.zst)
   Contains packages under their own licenses. License texts are kept inside the
   image under /usr/share/licenses/. This repository adds no restrictions on top
   of those licenses.

3. kona-ctl (prebuilt/kona-ctl)
   Prebuilt aarch64 ALSA control tool, used by kona-audio-init. Source is not
   available and its license is unknown. If you need a clean set, remove it and
   replace the kona-audio-init calls with amixer equivalents
   (see docs/system-services.md).

4. Qt 6.12 and Mesa/Turnip
   tools/qt-patch.py and tools/tb371fc-turnip-kgsl-patch only contain byte offsets
   and patch logic. No Qt or Mesa binaries are redistributed by this repository.

5. Everything else in this repository
   Code: MIT (see LICENSE).
   Documentation under docs/: CC BY-SA 4.0.
